 <paragraph index="897" node_type="writer">NEGOTIATE_DATALINK- 254</paragraph>
 <paragraph index="898" node_type="writer">	A datalink control message, exclusively used by the radio ingest device. A channel hop is used when a channel that is in use is of low quality.</paragraph>
 <paragraph index="899" node_type="writer">	The information provided by the DATALINK_TELEMETRY is used to determine the quality of the channel in use. A channel hop may also be purposefully triggered by the user.</paragraph>
 <paragraph index="900" node_type="writer">	In the current version, channel options must be set up before code compilation.</paragraph>
